<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Joanot Martorell</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1410–<a href="/years/1465">1465</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Joanot Martorell was a Valencian knight and writer of the 15th century, the main author of the chivalric romance <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tirant-lo-blanc">Tirant lo Blanc</a>. Written in Catalan and published at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a> in 1490, after his death, the book follows a Breton knight who saves the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>. Its realism and humour were praised by Cervantes in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/don-quixote">Don Quixote</a>, and it is counted among the masterpieces of Catalan literature.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/joanot-martorell.jpg" alt="Joanot Martorell" width="320" height="469" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonymous · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tirante_el_Blanco_1511.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
